# The finned example rocket solved by the 3D engine with the viscous terms (BOWSHOCK_ENGINE=3d, RANS on the GPU): the fin sector at zero incidence and the half domain at
# 6 degrees, in the 3D scene of the whole rocket: the eddy-viscosity ratio on a meridian sheet through a fin plane, and the skin friction on the walls. A real solve (a
# few minutes on the GPU: the headless driver waits for it), through the queue:
#   tools/gpuq/gpuq submit --host local --name finned-3d-viscous -- env BOWSHOCK_ENGINE=3d ICED_TEST_BACKEND=wgpu \
#     cargo run --release -q -p bowshock -- drive --example crates/bowshock/scripts/finned-3d-viscous.drive out/finned-3d-viscous
viewport 1500x1100
click "Analyze"
click "CFD table"
click "Flow field"
move (100, 1000)
move (102, 1002)
screenshot sector-default-dark.png

click "Fin plane"
click "Eddy ratio"
move (100, 1000)
move (102, 1002)
screenshot sector-eddy-ratio-fin-plane-dark.png

click "Skin friction"
move (100, 1000)
move (102, 1002)
screenshot sector-skin-friction-eddy-dark.png

# the half domain at 6 degrees (the angle stepper: 0, 2, 6)
click "▶"
click "▶"
click "Fin plane"
move (100, 1000)
move (102, 1002)
screenshot half-6deg-skin-friction-eddy-dark.png
click "Mach"
click "Wall Cp"
move (100, 1000)
move (102, 1002)
screenshot half-6deg-mach-wall-cp-dark.png
